<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding — Model fidelity to source: 58/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-19"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Computes analytic bilayer pouch dome curvature kappa_dome from apical-vs-basal differential growth and basal ECM stiffness (L48-63), backed by 3 Lean 4 theorems in `Loop_049_wing_disc_dome_folding.lean`. However, `generate_analytic_wing_disc_profile` (L66-92) uses a closed-form Gaussian ansatz rather than solving the 2D sagittal apico-basal bilayer morphoelastic energy functional F = F_e * F_g via L-BFGS-B." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:evidenceAgainst "2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py L66–L92: Closed-form 1D Gaussian-cleft + parabolic-dome ansatz rather than L-BFGS-B morphoelastic energy minimization <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/e93f00e/2020-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding.py#L66-L92>" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-model-fidelity-1> ;
    pk:hasScore 5.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "partially faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-tozluoglu-wing-disc-dome-folding-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Tozluoglu et al. (2019) Dev. Cell & Sui et al. (2018) Nat. Commun. Drosophila wing imaginal disc planar differential growth, basal ECM dome & H/N, H/H, H/P hinge folding — Morphometric validation: 54/100" ;
